# Project invariants

- Never commit secrets. Use `wrangler secret put` or `.dev.vars` (gitignored) for `LOGIN_USERNAME`, `LOGIN_PASSWORD`, `SHADOW_API_TOKEN`, and `CUSTOMER_SNAPSHOT_SYNC_SECRET`. Values in `wrangler.toml` are local-dev placeholders only.
- Never commit Routeware report exports (`*.csv`) — they contain real customer/address/container PII. They are gitignored.
- Do not log cookie headers, passwords, or full upstream request/response bodies in production code paths.
- Upstream Routeware session cookies live only in the `AuthSession` Durable Object and are never relayed to clients (upstream `Set-Cookie` is stripped in `upstreamForward.ts`).
- All `/api/v1/*` routes require `Authorization: Bearer <SHADOW_API_TOKEN>` except `GET /api/v1/health`. Privileged snapshot/data routes additionally require `CUSTOMER_SNAPSHOT_SYNC_SECRET`. Compare secrets in constant time (`src/lib/auth.ts`).
- The `X-Routeware-Shadow-Internal` marker is set only by trusted server-side callers via `forwardToUpstream`'s `internalMarker` option — never copied from client input.
- Prefer explicit `/api/v1/...` routes with fixed upstream URL templates over echoing arbitrary client path segments toward `/WebRW`.
